{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"upbeat-measly-arawana","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Why\n\nBug 449f-f9bf-be90-47fe fixed two Reconcile Bridge failure modes in code (landed as bcd888352, Gerrit 1072), proven by RED->GREEN unit oracles with mutation checks. What code tests cannot prove is that the failures stop occurring in production — that needs a post-fix run sample, which did not exist at close time because the fix had just landed.\n\nThis task carries that measurement so 449f does not stay open indefinitely waiting on wall-clock, and so the verification is not silently dropped.\n\n## What to measure\n\nOver a window of >= 500 `Reconcile Bridge` runs after 2026-07-31T00:30Z:\n\n- Mode 1 (lock-lease loss): zero runs failing with `reconcile heartbeat lost the lease` / `pass lock lease lost mid-pass`. Expect these to now appear as `::notice::Reconcile rescheduled (exit 75)` on a GREEN run instead of a red one — confirm the notice IS appearing, so we know the path is being exercised and not merely absent.\n- Mode 3 (outbound 404): zero runs failing with `reconcile_once raised: HTTP Error 404`. If a 404 occurs, confirm it is recorded as a per-mutation `stale-binding-404` outcome and the pass continued.\n\nEvidence: `gh run list --workflow=reconcile-bridge.yml` inventory with counts, plus the specific run ids for any mode-1 notice observed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A post-fix sample of >= 500 Reconcile Bridge runs is inventoried and recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Zero failures attributable to mode 1 (lock-lease loss) in that window.\n- [ ] Zero failures attributable to mode 3 (outbound 404 aborting the pass) in that window.\n- [ ] The mode-1 benign path is confirmed EXERCISED (an exit-75 notice observed), not merely absent — otherwise the sample proves nothing about it.\n- [ ] If any recurrence is found, a bug is filed and linked rather than the criterion being waived.","id":"597e-511c-0e0f-420d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Post-fix production verification: confirm Reconcile Bridge mode-1/mode-3 failures stop recurring"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785457353606100001,"uuid":"a26916f0-5fb7-44b0-8d05-cea97f8e4cb8"}